Multi-atom cross-module reference: `M.marker` has several atoms, and the
cross-module reference must resolve to its binding id alone, so the consumer's
rule fires whichever atoms a merge keeps on the element.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml m.re > m.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl m.ml -o m.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml n.re > n.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl n.ml -o n.ml

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml n.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a4hT1uK_l{background:red;}
  ._a7fWWIiyT{color:white;}
  ._cfyLsHzqtxfT9-b._iVOT1Gbzy{padding:1rem;}
